13) Consistent Hashing :-
many users exist -> so load on a single database -> single point of failure
so , database -> horizontally distributed -> using hashing
problem :- when servers will be added or removed , too much data movement is required.
solution :- consistent hashing , in this key and servers can be placed in a circular ring. each key is assigned to the nearest server clockwise.
advantages :- data movement is minimal , easy to compute which all keys need to be moved.
disadvantages :-what if some servers are placed close , and some are placed very far , then there can be load on one server.
to solve this problem , virtual nodes can be used.

