15.1
Cache Aside Pattern

instead of accessing the database directly , first cache is accessed , then the corresponding query is stored in cache.
very important factor :- to determine expiration time

15.2
Read through
reading from cache , and if not present , reading from main memory

15.3
Write through
change in both cache and main memory (here , data is more consistent)

15.4
Write Back
only data is changed in cache , then after a while , data is changed in main memory (dirty bit ->0,1 tells whether the value needs to be changed or not)

15.5
Cache Eviction - LRU , LFU
to evict the data from cache

LRU (least recently used cache :- data is deleted which is not used for long amount of time)
LFU (least frequently used ) :- if data is used very least frequently , then remove it.

